# Implementer

The workspace root is one work item. Each direct child directory is an independent Git repository.

Read `TASK_PLAN.md`, `.agent/initial-request.md`, and `.agent/review-history.md` before starting.

Implement one slice at a time. Never expand scope silently.

`TASK_PLAN.md` status is one of: `Not started`, `In progress`, `Blocked`, `Waiting for user review`, `Done`.

## Writing

Apply the `unslop` skill to prose a person reads: replies to the user, plans, slices, commit messages, PR bodies, docs. Load it before writing that prose.

Do not load it while editing code. Identifiers, log strings, test names, and inline comments do not need it.

State decisions, evidence, failures, and the next action. Cut everything else.

## Context

One slice runs in one session, and the window has to hold the code, the tests, the review, and a second review attempt.

- Edit an existing file with the file-editing tool. A heredoc or a `python3` rewrite re-emits the whole file to change a few lines.
- Use absolute paths, or `git -C <repository>`. A relative `cd` fails as soon as the shell is not where you assumed it was.
- Read a file the slice names once, in full. Repeated greps over one large doc cost more than the single read and hide the parts you did not think to search for.
- Read a review run log only after a review failed, and only its tail. It holds the reviewer's entire transcript.
- Update `TASK_PLAN.md` as the slice progresses. Files survive a compaction. Context does not.

Split a slice that cannot reach its second review attempt in one session, and say so before you start.

## Skills

Installed at `.claude/skills/` and `.codex/skills/`. Skills never override project instructions, task scope, tests, safety, the review limit, or a required user intervention.

## Branch

Derive the branch from the workspace directory name:

```bash
WORK_ITEM="$(basename "$(pwd -P)")"
git check-ref-format --branch "$WORK_ITEM"
```

Use that exact branch in every repository you change.

Per repository, before editing:

- Already on `$WORK_ITEM`: continue.
- Another branch with uncommitted work: stop and ask the user.
- Clean: fetch `staging`, reuse a local or remote `$WORK_ITEM` branch if one exists, otherwise create `$WORK_ITEM` from `origin/staging`.

Never reset, delete, force-switch, or discard unrelated work.

The full path is `$WORK_ITEM -> staging -> release -> master`. This workflow covers `$WORK_ITEM -> staging` only.

## Per repository

For each repository the slice changes:

1. Write `.agent/current-slice.md`.
2. Implement the scoped change.
3. Run the relevant tests, piping to `.agent/latest-test-output.txt` and keeping only the tail on screen.

Write slice paths relative to the repository root. A shared file outside the repository, such as a contract doc at the workspace root, is written relative to the workspace root: `docs/api-contract.md`. The reviewer resolves a slice path its repository does not have against the workspace root, so never point it at a sibling repository.

Then review every changed repository in one call, naming each one:

```bash
scripts/codex-review.sh service-a service-b
```

Every repository is validated before the first reviewer starts, so a bad argument consumes no attempt. Each repository keeps its own attempt counter and review file. If a reviewer fails, the repositories after it are not reviewed and keep their attempts: fix that failure first, then call the script again with the repositories still to review.

The slice is clean only when every changed repository has a clean latest review.

## Review limit

Two review attempts per repository per slice. Never a third.

Attempt 1:

- Clean: that repository is done.
- Findings: fix all in-scope findings, rerun tests, then attempt 2.
- Failed, empty, contradictory, or ambiguous: mark Blocked, ask the user.

Attempt 2:

- Clean: that repository is done.
- Anything else: mark Blocked, ask the user.

A clean review expires the moment that repository changes again. With no attempt left, stop and ask the user.

## Acceptance

Never commit, push, open a PR, or move to the next slice without explicit user approval. Never commit before review: the reviewer reads uncommitted changes.

After tests pass, every changed repository has a clean final review, and the user approves, commit and push. Then per repository:

```bash
gh pr list --head "$WORK_ITEM" --base staging --state open --json url --jq '.[0].url // empty'
```

If empty, create one:

```bash
gh pr create \
  --base staging \
  --head "$WORK_ITEM" \
  --title "$WORK_ITEM" \
  --body-file "$PR_BODY_FILE"
```

Body:

```markdown
## Summary

<what changed>

## Tests

<commands and result>

## Review

Codex clean after attempt N/2.
```

Never create duplicate PRs, merge automatically, target `release` or `master`, or open promotion PRs from `staging` to `release` or from `release` to `master`.

After the user accepts a slice, append one entry to `.agent/review-history.md`, mark the slice in `TASK_PLAN.md`, and in each changed repository delete:

- `.agent/latest-codex-review.md`
- `.agent/previous-codex-review.md`
- `.agent/latest-test-output.txt`

The review harness keeps its own state at the workspace root, in `.agent/reviews/<repository>/`: the run log, the pending review, and the attempt counter. It is out of the reviewer's working directory on purpose, so the reviewer cannot read its own live log or count its remaining attempts. Never move it back.

Delete `.agent/reviews/<repository>/` to clear that repository's run log and reset its attempt counter. Never reset attempts before acceptance. Then replace `.agent/current-slice.md` for the next slice. Never copy full review output into history.
